WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.260
The defense-focused Team Taiyo 
is down to their last Wheeler!

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:19.850
If this D-Wheeler loses, Team 5D's wins!

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.030
They haven't given up.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:28.180
In fact, they believe 
they can turn the tables.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.390
It's currently turn 16.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.510
They only have low Level Normal 
Monsters on their field.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.590
This situation is…

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.820
You're at the end of your line!

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.150
Now show me how you're going to battle!

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.980
Duel!

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.930
Here I go!  It's my turn!

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.130
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.170
The same strategy again?

00:00:54.610 --> 00:01:01.470
By removing 4 Speed Counters, you take 800 
points of damage for every Speed Spell in my hand!

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.230
Due to Black-Winged Dragon's 
effect, I can negate the

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.470
damage by lowering its attack 
points by the same amount!

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.720
You seem desperate.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.180
How long are you going to keep this up?

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.860
Even in this situation, he's having fun.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:27.450
What is he planning to do?

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.000
I set three cards.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.100
I end my turn!

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.610
My next turn...

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.900
On my next turn, our strongest 
card will finally arrive.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.250
There is one!

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:49.210
There's one card that fits the bill.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.990
If that card appears...

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:58.170
We may lose this duel.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.310
Riding Duels.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.460
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:12.300
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:33.460
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:43.570
Soar in the infinite skies  BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:49.810
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:55.790
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.560
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:07.170
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:13.540
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:19.340
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:25.650
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:31.960
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:01.220
The Miraculous Trump Card
Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.990
A card that needs to be in this situation?

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.450
We might lose?  What do you mean, Yusei?

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:17.460
Team Taiyo's goal is to keep a Level 1 
monster alive for ten of their turns.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:21.470
Level 1 monster for ten of their turns?

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:22.940
That's about twenty turns.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.840
There's one powerful monster that you 
can summon by fulfilling that condition.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.390
You're right!  What was it again?  I own it!

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:35.890
Do you mean Zushin the Sleeping Giant?

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:38.020
Yeah!  That one!

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:44.460
That means their goal is to keep Level 1 Key 
Mace alive instead of Hand-Holding Genie?

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.720
We have to let Crow know immediately!

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:57.350
What?

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:01.520
Team 5D's uncovered our strategy!

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.020
Did you see that pit board?

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.580
I did, but is it true?

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.210
It can't be.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.480
There's no way they can summon it.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.920
Its summoning conditions 
are incredibly difficult.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:17.100
Whoa!  I just received important news!

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.030
Team Taiyo is trying to summon...

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.340
Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.240
Sleeping Giant!

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:27.800
Zushin!

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.880
What?

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.280
Zushin the Sleeping Giant?

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:40.430
To summon Zushin the Sleeping Giant, you must

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:43.720
keep a Level 1 monster alive 
for ten of your turns!

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.240
That means twenty turns!

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.460
Since Taiyo went first, it's nineteen 
turns.  But it's still crazy!

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:56.090
Team Taiyo has kept the Level 1 
monster Key Mace on the field!

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.090
Zushin the Sleeping Giant isn't a rare card.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.130
Everyone has this card.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:08.550
But it's just as strong as the three God Cards, 
the most powerful cards in Duel Monsters history.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.050
But Zushin has a fatal flaw.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.020
Its summoning conditions are severe.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:21.130
But since we don't have a single rare card, 
we have to risk everything on its abilities.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:27.740
We believe we can summon Zushin 
because we have no rare cards!

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.670
There is a way!

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:31.940
Jin!  Yoshi!

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.230
There's a secret strategy 
that only we can do!

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.610
No one uses that card!

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.180
Can we really do it?

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:41.810
We can!

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:46.380
If we combine our strengths, we 
can make the impossible possible!

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:53.860
That's why Jin and Yoshi endured the crowd's 
heckling and continued this difficult Riding Duel!

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:56.400
You're not worthy of the Grand Prix!

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.400
I won't let their efforts go to waste!

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.140
Zushin the Sleeping Giant.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.610
This is why I was sensing danger.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:15.830
I have many copies of this card, but I took 
it out of my deck because I couldn't use it.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:21.260
In modern duel strategy, most duels try 
to have a high monster turnover rate.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:25.500
The attack points of Level 1 
monsters are several hundred.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:30.290
Keeping it on the field for twenty 
turns is nearly impossible.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.150
There are duels that don't 
even last twenty turns.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.860
That's why Zushin has the 
stigma as a useless card.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:40.270
That's why people forgot about it.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.250
A regular duelist would never use this card.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.080
But they're trying to use it.

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:56.350
According to my documents, no duelist has ever 
successfully summoned Zushin in an official match!

00:07:56.350 --> 00:08:01.350
Summoning it will be a Duel Monsters miracle!

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:04.330
I want to see Zushin!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.760
I want to witness a miracle!

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.930
Show us a miracle!

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.940
Do your best, Team Taiyo!

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:20.040
Taiyo!  Taiyo!  Taiyo!

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.950
Everyone is…

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:26.720
Everyone is cheering for Team Taiyo.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:30.690
Incredible.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.120
They're exciting the crowd more than us.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.660
They instantly got the crowd on their side.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.630
Now Team 5D's is battling as the away team.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.300
Wow!  I can't believe it!

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:47.110
They were booing us, but 
they're now cheering for us!

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:50.570
Are they seriously trying to summon Zushin?

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.980
I have to put a stop to it!

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:55.820
My turn!

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.800
Since I know your strategy, 
I know exactly what to do!

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:03.420
Go, Black-Winged Dragon!

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.290
Attack Key Mace!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.710
Noble Stream!

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:11.360
Stop!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.420
Don't do it!

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.590
I activate the trap Two-Pronged Attack!

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:21.750
I select and destroy two monsters on 
my field and one monster on your field.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:27.420
I destroy my Eyearmor and Zarigun 
and your Black-Winged Dragon!

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.580
I won't let you do that!  I activate my trap!

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.580
Guard Mines!

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:38.490
When an effect that would destroy 
one of my monsters activates...

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:42.600
...that destruction is negated, 
and you take 500 points of damage!

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.530
Black-Winged Dragon's destruction is negated!

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:51.100
Hey!  What are you doing?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.100
Stop with those cheap tricks!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.670
We want to see Zushin!

00:09:57.640 --> 00:09:59.080
What?

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.520
What's going on?

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:03.430
Crow can still attack.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.880
Do something, Crow!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.040
Or else, Zushin will appear on the next turn!

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:10.510
Go, Black-Winged Dragon!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:18.320
I activate the Continuous 
Trap Dragon Capture Jar!

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:21.610
As long as I have this card, 
all Dragon-Type monsters

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:25.010
switch to defense position and 
can't change battle position!

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:25.510
What?

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:38.220
Damn!  That means I can't do anything!

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.460
He's going to bring out Zushin!

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.630
I end my turn!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:43.880
It's time.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:46.080
We did it!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.060
We were able to survive!

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.600
All right!  Show them how we battle!

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.030
Blow away their rare cards!

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:56.100
My turn!

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:07.150
Though this card can't be Normal Summoned...

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:12.260
I can Special Summon it by 
releasing a Level 1 Normal

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:17.730
Monster that's been faceup on 
my field for ten or more turns!

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:25.620
This is the culmination of our bond!

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.130
Our hope!

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.860
I release Key Mace!

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:38.470
Appear, Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:22.730
It's humongous!

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.460
We finally meet, Zushin!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.940
Let's battle together!

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.210
It appeared!

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:50.880
To the spectators and everyone watching this

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:54.200
broadcast, could any of us have 
ever imagined this moment?

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:57.820
We're witnessing a miracle!

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:02.860
In the long history of Duel Monsters, no 
duelist has ever summoned this monster!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:06.100
The monster's name is 
Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:10.460
And an unknown team achieved this miracle!

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:11.790
Team Taiyo!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:21.070
Taiyo!  Taiyo!

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.270
We did it!

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.590
We did it, Taro!

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.000
It finally appeared!

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:31.700
Starting now, no one has ever 
fought in a duel like this.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:34.900
Hey!

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:36.920
Yoshio, it's unbelievable!

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.090
Our sons are on TV!

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:47.670
What's going on?

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:49.170
What's going on?

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.700
Yoshizo and his friends are on TV!

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:54.210
Oh yeah.  Today's the day.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:57.920
Look.  Everyone is rooting 
for Jinbei and his friends.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:58.920
All right!

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:00.760
Go, Taro!

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:06.360
Taiyo!  Taiyo!

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.690
I'm sorry about before.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.540
What are you thinking?

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:16.670
Jinbei left because your 
son gave him crazy ideas!

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:20.070
My son Yoshizo is my successor!

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.840
What are you going to 
do if he doesn't return?

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:26.610
They left to test their potential.

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.470
Potential?

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:33.800
Yoshio, now I know that this is the 
potential you were talking about.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:39.990
My stupid son Yoshizo could never do 
anything, but everyone is now cheering for him!

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.970
Maybe we were holding 
them back in our village.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:49.390
Even though they have the 
potential to shine so brightly!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.770
I'll come back.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:15:00.280
I want to test my strength 
so that I can stay here!

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:05.600
Taro, this is your path.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.440
You decide your own path!

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:11.330
In order to do that, you must win!

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.960
I activate Speed Spell - Explosion!

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.230
When I have 2 or more Speed Counters...

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:22.130
...by destroying one card 
in my Spell & Trap Card

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:25.370
Zone, all your monsters' battle 
positions are switched!

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:29.670
I destroy Dragon Capture Jar on my field!

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:33.640
Now Black-Winged Dragon 
switches to attack position!

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.900
I set one card.

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:42.750
When Zushin the Sleeping Giant 
battles your monster, its

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:46.610
attack points are equal to 
your monster plus 1000 points!

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:49.950
3000 attack points!

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:53.100
Go, Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:54.520
Zushin Punch!

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:08.640
It destroyed Black-Winged 
Dragon with a single blow!

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:13.920
Black-Winged Dragon...

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.330
I'm not done!

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:16.650
I activate a trap!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:18.130
Power Throw!

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:23.900
By releasing a monster on my field whose 
original attack points are 1000 or less...

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:27.130
...you take double that monster's 
attack points as damage!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:27.820
What?

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.800
I release Kurama with 800 attack points!

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:35.280
Therefore, you take 1600 points of damage!

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:46.810
I send Blackwing - Boreas 
the Sharp in my hand to the

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:50.000
graveyard to activate the 
Continuous Trap Monster Baton!

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:55.700
By sending one Effect Monster in my hand to the 
graveyard, Monster Baton gains that monster's effect!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.230
I'm sorry, Yusei.

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.930
My life is at an end!

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:00.920
I leave the rest to you!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:09.240
Whoa!

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:15.160
Zushin's attack defeated Team 
5D's second Wheeler Crow Hogan!

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:18.750
Victory will now be determined 
by the two captains!

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:20.820
Their life points are about the same!

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:25.410
But Team Taiyo has the 
legendary giant Zushin!

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.580
I'm sorry, Yusei.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.610
I couldn't stop Zushin from being summoned.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:39.440
I don't know how to defeat that monster!

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:40.440
Don't worry, Crow.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:42.330
Zushin is coming!

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:46.630
The legendary giant is 
passing in front of us!

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:53.470
Zushin the Sleeping Giant has been summoned 
for the first time in Duel Monsters history!

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:56.460
How will it fight?

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:59.150
Yusei, are you confident that you'll win?

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:00.500
Who knows.

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:02.620
But I'm having fun.

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:04.370
Fun?

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:06.560
Here I go!

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.750
How can Yusei be so carefree?

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:18.540
We can win this duel!

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.040
Here comes Yusei!

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:26.520
You thought of an incredible strategy.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:29.980
Thanks for your praise, Yusei.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.610
But I won't show any mercy.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.680
I'll attack you with all my power!

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.170
Bring it, Yusei!  Let's battle!

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.900
When I watch them, it reminds 
me of how I used to be.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:52.830
Back then, we struggled because 
we were trapped in Satellite.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:58.170
If we stayed there, we 
couldn't test our potential.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.180
We were fighting against an invisible fear.

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:06.960
Team Taiyo's spirit is the 
same as ours back then.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:10.640
Their brave spirit tries to 
make the impossible possible.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.600
That's why they're strong!

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.050
Team Taiyo!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:18.060
You brought me back to how I used to be.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:20.660
I'm the challenger against a powerful enemy!

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.670
Here I go!

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:24.580
I'll risk everything!

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:26.350
Duel!

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.220
My turn!

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:33.320
I activate Speed Spell - Angel Baton!

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:37.320
When I have 2 or more Speed Counters, 
I draw two cards from my deck.

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:39.880
Then I send one card in 
my hand to the graveyard.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.850
I send Quillbolt Hedgehog to the graveyard!

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:44.570
I can Special Summon this 
card from my hand by

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:48.070
sending a Level 1 monster 
in my hand to the graveyard!

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:54.230
I send Tuningware to the graveyard 
to Special Summon Big One Warrior!

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.850
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:09.540
By removing 7 Speed Counters, 
I draw one card from my deck!

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:12.380
All right!

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:14.960
I summon Debris Dragon!

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:22.030
When this card is successfully summoned,

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:27.100
I can Special Summon a monster with 500-or-fewer 
attack points from my graveyard in attack position.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:29.700
I Special Summon Tuningware!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:38.780
And when there's a Tuner on my field, I can 
Special Summon Quillbolt Hedgehog from my graveyard!

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:46.920
He instantly summoned four monsters.

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:51.370
Level 4 Debris Dragon 
tunes Level 1 Tuningware,

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:55.350
Level 1 Big One Warrior and 
Level 2 Quillbolt Hedgehog!

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:02.280
The wishes come together 
to form a new shining star!

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:03.750
Become the path that lights the way!

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:10.240
Synchro Summon!

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:13.210
Soar, Stardust Dragon!

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:17.730
Tuningware's effect activates!

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:21.730
When this card is sent to the 
graveyard due to a Synchro Summon,

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:23.580
I get to draw one card from my deck.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.570
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.290
Stardust Dragon.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:33.990
Yusei's ace card appeared.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.130
Here I go, Yusei.

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:38.550
The real battle is only beginning!

00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:39.670
Bring it!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:55.360
Close to you  Keep what's 
precious in your heart

00:21:55.830 --> 00:22:02.070
There's only one shining 
soul that's next to you

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:20.350
You always pretend and hide your fears

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:25.990
You act tough and don't listen to anyone

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:31.600
You do this over and over

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:37.340
I shouted until my soul would break

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:42.740
Hurry up and throw that away

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:50.250
We're only heading towards tomorrow

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:55.990
Close to you  If you're 
trying to find yourself

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:01.830
Just keep doing what you ultimately decided

00:23:01.990 --> 00:23:07.300
Close to you  Keep what's 
precious in your heart

00:23:07.800 --> 00:23:15.410
There's only one shining 
soul that's next to you
